From 742c7031d2dd0267fa3fe063ea14af04723d7524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:48:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A clip can come from another character model, retargeted onto
 the unit's own skeleton

PlayUnitAnimation's ninth argument names a character model ("ScourgeFemale", "OrcMale"...) or
a model's path: its take on the clip is retargeted onto the unit's skeleton once per model and
played like one of its own. The bones pair by their KeyBoneID, then outward and inward from
those along the tree by the way each points at rest; each paired bone's turns carry over as
they are (a vanilla M2's rest pose is unrotated), the hips' travel is scaled to the unit's
height, and every other bone keeps its own length. The borrowed clips live in the rig's
ExtraClips (PoseExtra), which the pose evaluator reads beside the model's own; the model loads
on first use (its own clip plays until it has), and PreloadAnimationSource(name) loads it
early. HasActionCombat() is 10.
